WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Muse, make no mistakes. Ask your agent to act, with Stardive checking the
result.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Here is a real Muse task. Write this welcome note and keep it under twenty
words. The original request is saved.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Muse uses separate work and check phases. The first agent saves the
request, creates the private draft, and uploads its version.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:34.000
A second LLM worker runs the checking phase. Stardive’s executable checks
compare the actual file with the saved requirements.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:46.000
The event graph links the recorded request, workers, artifact, review,
receipt, and release. These are selected evidence links, replayed with
compressed timing.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:56.000
This receipt belongs to this task and file version. The published file
matches the checked snapshot: forty-nine bytes.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
When a required check fails, the workflow holds the file back. This
recorded control shows an unchanged word limit blocking delivery.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Stardive. Check the work. Keep your intent. A receipt for what was actually
checked.
